      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 02 – Training and Feature Importance\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook is a companion to the scripted training pipeline in\n",
        "`pipelines/train_model.py`. It is intentionally lightweight so that the\n",
        "core logic lives in versioned Python code, while this notebook provides\n",
        "an interactive place to:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Inspect the engineered feature tables under `data/processed/feature_tables/`\n",
        "- Run the training pipeline and reload artifacts from `models/`\n",
        "- Explore feature importance and calibration diagnostics\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        \"%load_ext autoreload\\n\",\n",
        \"%autoreload 2\\n\",\n",
        "\\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "\\n",
        "from pipelines import train_model\n",
        "\\n",
        "DATA_DIR = Path(\"data/processed\")\n",
        "FEATURE_TABLE_DIR = DATA_DIR / \"feature_tables\"\n",
        "MODELS_DIR = Path(\"models\")\n",
        "\\n",
        "FEATURE_TABLE_DIR, MODELS_DIR"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Run scripted training (optional)\n",
        "\n",
        "You can run the training pipeline from the notebook for convenience, or\n",
        "invoke it from the command line instead:\n",
        "\n",
        "```bash\n",
        "python pipelines/train_model.py \\\n",
        "  --transactions_path data/processed/transactions_clean.parquet \\\n",
        "  --feature_service_name risk_scoring_v1 \\\n",
        "  --sample_rows 200000 \\\n",
        "  --out_dir models\n",
        "```\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Example: run training from the notebook (optional)\n",
        "train_model.main([\n",
        "    \"--transactions_path\", \"data/processed/transactions_clean.parquet\",\n",
        "    \"--feature_service_name\", \"risk_scoring_v1\",\n",
        "    \"--sample_rows\", \"200000\",\n",
        "    \"--out_dir\", \"models\",\n",
        "])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Load model artifacts\n",
        "\n",
        "After training, you can inspect `models/model_metadata.json` and\n",
        "`models/feature_importance.csv` here for interactive analysis and plots."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import json\n",
        "from pprint import pprint\n",
        "\\n",
        "metadata_path = MODELS_DIR / \"model_metadata.json\"\n",
        "importance_path = MODELS_DIR / \"feature_importance.csv\"\n",
        "\\n",
        "if metadata_path.exists():\n",
        "    with open(metadata_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "        meta = json.load(f)\n",
        "    print(\"Model metadata loaded from\", metadata_path)\n",
        "    pprint(meta[\"metrics\"][\"validation\"])\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"No model_metadata.json found; run the training pipeline first.\")\n",
        "\\n",
        "if importance_path.exists():\n",
        "    imp = pd.read_csv(importance_path)\n",
        "    imp.head()\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"No feature_importance.csv found; run the training pipeline first.\")"
      ]
    }
  ],
